555
00:42:43,861 --> 00:42:48,140
And then about a half hour later, a third one came

556
00:42:48,141 --> 00:42:52,351
in and crashed into the forward right with the focus hole.

557
00:42:52,352 --> 00:42:54,820
And that was the most damaging hit

558
00:42:54,821 --> 00:43:01,960
in terms of people killed because we had people out on deck there and he sprayed gasoline, flaming

559
00:43:01,961 --> 00:43:09,941
gas, all over that forward deck. With its hull almost torn in two, the bush sank.

560
00:43:09,942 --> 00:43:11,320
87 of its crew

561
00:43:11,321 --> 00:43:17,440
members went with it.

562
00:43:17,441 --> 00:43:23,000
In the weeks that followed, the destroyers faced more than 1,500 kamikaze attacks.

563
00:43:23,001 --> 00:43:26,980
By the war's end, they had fought in nearly every naval battle.

564
00:43:26,981 --> 00:43:32,440
In total, over 1,300 battle stars were awarded to the Fletcher class.

565
00:43:32,441 --> 00:43:36,580
But a bigger accolade awaited them.

566
00:43:36,581 --> 00:43:43,580
In August 1945, Admiral Bull Halsey ordered that three destroyers, the USS Nicholas, O'Bannon

567
00:43:43,581 --> 00:43:49,640
and Taylor, accompany the mighty battleship Missouri to accept Japan's surrender because

568
00:43:49,641 --> 00:43:56,380
of their valorous fight of the long road from the South Pacific to the very end.

569
00:43:56,381 --> 00:44:02,040
We met the Japanese destroyer that came out of Tokyo Bay with the harbor pilots and peace

570
00:44:02,041 --> 00:44:06,300
emissaries and we sent our whale boat over there and picked them up and then

571
00:44:06,301 --> 00:44:12,840
transferred to them to the Missouri and to other ships in the fleet it was quite

572
00:44:12,841 --> 00:44:15,180
an honor

573
00:44:15,181 --> 00:44:21,420
by the end of World War two 175 of these tough destroyers had been built and

574
00:44:21,421 --> 00:44:26,600
sent into battle 25 had been lost

575
00:44:26,601 --> 00:44:35,400
The halls of steel are long gone, but for the men of the destroyers, the fighting spirit lives on.

576
00:44:36,060 --> 00:44:37,360
Thank God for the Fletchers.

577
00:44:38,460 --> 00:44:41,080
It was the finest destroyer that was ever built.

578
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:44,180
Be a captain of a destroyer.

579
00:44:44,320 --> 00:44:46,120
You're a king in your own world.

